Hi Jennifer,

Before we meet this afternoon, I wanted to put the handoff situations we have=
 been hearing about in one place.

A delivery window can change while the earlier window is still the one passed=
 to the next dispatcher. A route can be marked Held without the reason making=
 it across the handoff. When a replacement vehicle is assigned, the number ma=
y be visible but the next dispatcher may not know whether the replacement is =
actually settled. And a Note on an exception stop can be skipped when the rou=
te is handed over.

Could the study follow the information the receiving person uses to make a de=
cision, rather than just asking the outgoing person to describe their steps? =
I would like to understand where the information comes from and what reaches =
the next person. The attached screen reference shows the current planning fie=
lds for our discussion.

Thanks,
Christine

Christine Wright
Design Lead
Oakridge Dispatch Cooperative


